---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../site.ts";
---
<Base title="About" description="What Virginia Energy Watch is, where its numbers come from, and what it is not.">
  <article class="band narrow prose">
    <h1>About this site</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      {SITE.name} helps Virginia households and the people who work with them answer three questions: how hard is my energy
      bill to pay, what is my utility asking the State Corporation Commission (SCC) for, and how do I weigh in before the deadline.
    </p>

    <h2>What's here now</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/">Energy burden map</a>: how much of their income households spend on home energy, for every county and
        independent city, by income level. The figures can be <a href="/data/va-burden-localities.csv">downloaded as CSV</a>.</li>
      <li><a href="/cases/">SCC cases</a>: a hand-picked list of electric and gas cases, with key dates, comment deadlines and
        links to the official filings. It is being filled in now.</li>
      <li><a href="/learn/glossary/">Glossary</a>: the rate-case terms that come up most, in plain English.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Coming next</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Census-tract detail and address search on the map.</li>
      <li>Which electric and gas utility serves each area.</li>
      <li>A rate-increase calculator: if rates rise by a given percent, how burden changes in your area.</li>
      <li>Plain-English explainers for the biggest open cases.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What this site is not</h2>
    <p>
      This is information, not legal advice. The site is not affiliated with the SCC, any utility or any advocacy
      organization. Case details are entered by hand from the public SCC record and can lag behind it; every case page links
      to the official record, which is always the source of truth.
    </p>

    <h2>How case information is gathered</h2>
    <p>
      Cases are tracked from the SCC's public Docket Search and entered by hand. The site does not run automated crawlers
      against the SCC's website.
    </p>

    <h2>Who made it</h2>
    <p>{SITE.byline} The code and data are open on <a href={SITE.repo}>GitHub</a>; corrections are welcome as issues there.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
